2. The canonical family has exactly two positive TT directions at every
   nonzero-spatial Nyquist stratum. Spatial zero momentum is a separate
   constraint/zero-mode stratum and cannot honestly be folded into that
   statement.

The first newly exposed physical choice is temporal. The constraint-preserving
